# Fault J-A-1: `unit(t.units.to)` as a key of the unit kind `funds` was refused `LOAD-KEY ... (unitkey) is not a key
# of funds`. L §5.10 Kind and unit: "a price keyed by unit is read at a leg's own key ... Where load can't see the key
# (a leg declared with a unit kind), it is read per value (§3.2)"; `unit(x)` of a one-unit place is its unit as a key.
# The buy's units go to h, of unit glb, and p[glb] = 2: both reads are 2 DUK/glb (q).
=== m.tally
model f
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
kind funds: unit
kind lots_in: event certain
  leg units: funds
source s "synthetic"
place h: holdings glb lives 2026-01-01..
place market: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input p[u in funds]: num DUK/u
input bday: date
input n: num
move buy: lots_in
  on bday
  leg units from market to h amount n * 1 glb
def jz[t in lots_in]: num DUK/glb = p[unit(t.units.to)]
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  funds + [glb] lives 2018-01-01..
  p[glb] = 2
  bday = 2026-02-01
  n = 3
ask q: p[unit(h)], jz[t] for t in lots_in over 2026
=== expect
q (t = buy): (2 DUK/glb, 2 DUK/glb)
  cut 2026-01-01
